verted-index#how-does-it-work","content":"With these indexes in place, queries become extremely efficient ✨:","locale":"en"},"1255":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-76","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#how-does-it-work","content":"\"Find all Italian recipes\" → look up \"Italian\" in the `cuisine` index → `[1, 4, 5]`","locale":"en"},"1256":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-77","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#how-does-it-work","content":"\"Show recipes by Marco Rossi\" → look up \"Marco Rossi\" in the `author` index → `[4, 5]`","locale":"en"},"1257":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-78","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#how-does-it-work","content":"\"Find Italian recipes by Julia Chen\" → intersect `[1, 4, 5]` and `[1, 6]` → `[1]`","locale":"en"},"1258":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-79","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#how-does-it-work","content":"We **do not index** `url`, because it's rarely used in queries. Indexing it would waste storage and slow down writes, with little benefit. Once we have a document ID, we can always fetch its `url` directly from the original data.","locale":"en"},"1259":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-80","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Because it inverts the standard mapping:","locale":"en"},"1260":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-81","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Direction","locale":"en"},"1261":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-82","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Mapping","locale":"en"},"1262":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-83","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Forward","locale":"en"},"1263":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-84","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Document ID → List of Terms","locale":"en"},"1264":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-85","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Inverted","locale":"en"},"1265":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-86","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"Term → List of Document IDs","locale":"en"},"1266":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-87","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#why-inverted","content":"This inversion is what makes keyword-based search efficient. Instead of checking every document to see if it contains your query term, you jump straight to the term and get all matching documents immediately.","locale":"en"},"1267":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-88","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#trade-offs","content":"While powerful, inverted indexes come with costs:","locale":"en"},"1268":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-89","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#trade-offs","content":"⚠️ **Storage overhead**: The index requires additional storage space.","locale":"en"},"1269":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index-90","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/inverted-index#trade-offs","content":"⚠️ **Write amplification**: Every write operation — `INSERT`, `UPSERT`, and `UPDATE` — require index maintenance, which adds latency to writes and increases I/O load.","locale":"en"},"1270":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"page","content":"Vector Embedding","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Introduction","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","locale":"en"},"1271":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","content":"A numerical representation of unstructured data that captures semantic meaning for similarity search.","locale":"en"},"1272":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-a-vector","content":"What is a Vector?","locale":"en"},"1273":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"How Do You Use Vectors with a Database?","locale":"en"},"1274":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"How Vectors Power Real-World Applications?","locale":"en"},"1275":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"What is an Embedding Model?","locale":"en"},"1276":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#types-of-vectors","content":"Types of Vectors","locale":"en"},"1277":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"Dense Vectors","locale":"en"},"1278":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"Sparse Vectors","locale":"en"},"1279":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-a-vector","content":"In the context of AI and vector databases, &#x2A;**a vector is a list of numbers generated by embedding models to capture the semantic essence of unstructured data*** —  such as text, images, or audio.","locale":"en"},"1280":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-a-vector","content":"These models transform raw input into a high-dimensional space where &#x2A;**semantically similar items produce similar vectors***, enabling AI systems to compare meaning rather than relying on exact word matches.","locale":"en"},"1281":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"🗂️ **Store**: Generate embeddings from your data — documents, product images, or user profiles — and save them in the vector database.","locale":"en"},"1282":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"🔍 **Search**: When a new query arrives (a question, photo, etc.), generate a **query vector** using the same embedding model, then ask the database to find the most similar vectors.","locale":"en"},"1283":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-do-you-use-vectors-with-a-database","content":"Using efficient indexes, the database quickly returns relevant results — even at large scale. This is the foundation of semantic search: **finding what &#x2A;**means**&#x2A; the same, not just what &#x2A;**says*** the same**.","locale":"en"},"1284":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"**Image search** is a great example:","locale":"en"},"1285":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"Each image is converted into a vector that captures its visual features — such as shape, color, and object type.","locale":"en"},"1286":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"Images that are **visually or semantically similar end up with nearby vectors**.","locale":"en"},"1287":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"By comparing these vectors, search systems can:","locale":"en"},"1288":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"✅ **Recognize the same person across different photos**: Even with changes in lighting, pose, or expression, images of one individual generate similar vectors, allowing the system to match identities reliably.","locale":"en"},"1289":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"✅ **Find look-alike products in e-commerce platforms**: When a user snaps a photo of a dress, lamp, or sofa, the system compares its vector to product vectors and retrieves items with similar appearance or style.","locale":"en"},"1290":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#how-vectors-power-real-world-applications","content":"All of this happens through fast vector similarity comparisons, powered by the vector database.","locale":"en"},"1291":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"An embedding model is an AI model that converts raw data into vector embeddings — illustrated in the diagram at the top.","locale":"en"},"1292":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"These models learn patterns from vast amounts of training data so that objects with similar meanings produce vectors that are close together in vector space — typically measured using distance metrics such as **cosine similarity**, **dot product**, or **Euclidean distance**.","locale":"en"},"1293":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"**The choice of distance metric matters.** If an embedding model was trained for a specific metric (e.g., cosine similarity), the vector database should use the same metric during search to preserve semantic relationships and achieve optimal accuracy.","locale":"en"},"1294":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#what-is-an-embedding-model","content":"To explore and compare state-of-the-art embedding models, you can check out the Embedding Leaderboard on Hugging Face, which evaluates hundreds of models across diverse tasks and languages.","locale":"en"},"1295":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#types-of-vectors","content":"Vector representations are primarily categorized into two types: &#x2A;**dense**&#x2A; and &#x2A;**sparse***, each capturing data in its own way.","locale":"en"},"1296":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"Dense vectors are fixed-length, real-valued embeddings where (nearly) every dimension carries semantic information. These vectors are often generated by deep learning models that transform raw inputs (e.g., text, images, audio) into a structured vector space reflecting their semantic similarities.","locale":"en"},"1297":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"**✅ Semantic-Rich**: understands context and meaning (e.g., \"king – man + woman ≈ queen\")","locale":"en"},"1298":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#dense-vectors","content":"**⚠️ Opaque**: hard to interpret which features drive similarity","locale":"en"},"1299":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"Sparse vectors are high-dimensional, often vocabulary-sized representations in which only a small subset of dimensions are non-zero. Each active dimension corresponds to a specific term (e.g., a word or n-gram), weighted by relevance scores such as **BM25**.","locale":"en"},"1300":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"In this model, every document is converted into a vector — called a document vector — that records which terms appear in it and how important they are. Similarly, a search query is also turned into a sparse vector using the same weighting scheme.","locale":"en"},"1301":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"Rather than relying on exact keyword matches, similarity between a query and a document is computed using the dot product of their vectors. This measures how well their weighted terms align: documents that contain the same important terms as the query receive higher scores — rewarding both **term overlap** and **term importance**.","locale":"en"},"1302":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"For computational efficiency, sparse vectors use integer indices to map terms to their positions within a vocabulary dictionary rather than storing the term strings directly.","locale":"en"},"1303":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"**✅ Interpretable**: non-zero dimensions map directly to known terms (e.g., `4017` → \"puppy\")","locale":"en"},"1304":{"id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/concepts/vector-embedding#sparse-vectors","content":"**⚠️ Lacks Semantic Understanding**: treats \"car\" and \"automobile\" as unrelated unless explicitly linked","locale":"en"},"1305":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","type":"page","content":"Delete","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","locale":"en"},"1306":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"Delete by IDs","locale":"en"},"1307":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-filter-condition","content":"Delete by Filter Condition","locale":"en"},"1308":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Zvec provides two ways to delete documents. Choose the method that best fits your use case:","locale":"en"},"1309":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Method","locale":"en"},"1310":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Input","locale":"en"},"1311":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"When to Use","locale":"en"},"1312":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"`delete()`","locale":"en"},"1313":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"One or more document `id`s","locale":"en"},"1314":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Use when you know the exact ID(s) of the documents you want to delete","locale":"en"},"1315":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"`delete_by_filter()`","locale":"en"},"1316":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"A filter expression (e.g., `publish_year < 1900`)","locale":"en"},"1317":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Use for bulk deletion based on field values — ideal for cleaning up documents that match specific criteria","locale":"en"},"1318":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","content":"Delete operations are **immediate** and **irreversible**.\\\nAlways double-check your input before running a delete operation.","locale":"en"},"1319":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"Assume you've already opened a collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1320":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"Use `delete()` to remove one or more documents when you know their exact IDs.","locale":"en"},"1321":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"When given a single `id`, `delete()` returns one `Status` object.","locale":"en"},"1322":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-ids","content":"When given a list of `id`s, it returns a list of `Status` objects in the same order.","locale":"en"},"1323":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-filter-condition","content":"Use `delete_by_filter()` to remove all documents that match a boolean `filter` expression.","locale":"en"},"1324":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/delete#delete-by-filter-condition","content":"The `filter` can reference scalar fields (e.g., `publish_year`, `language`) using comparison and logical operators.","locale":"en"},"1325":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","type":"page","content":"Fetch","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","locale":"en"},"1326":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"Use `fetch()` to retrieve documents by their `id`s.\\\nThis is a **direct lookup** — no search, scoring, or filtering is involved.","locale":"en"},"1327":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"**Input**: A single document `id` or a list of document `id`s.","locale":"en"},"1328":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"**Output**: A mapping from each **found** `id` to its corresponding document object.","locale":"en"},"1329":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"Missing `id`s are **silently omitted** from the result (no error raised).","locale":"en"},"1330":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/fetch","content":"The returned dictionary does not guarantee input order — access documents by `id` instead.","locale":"en"},"1331":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","type":"page","content":"Data Operations","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","locale":"en"},"1332":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Zvec provides a complete set of **data manipulation operations** to manage documents in your collection.","locale":"en"},"1333":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Operation","locale":"en"},"1334":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"1335":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Insert`","locale":"en"},"1336":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Add new documents (fails if the document `ID` already exists)","locale":"en"},"1337":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Upsert`","locale":"en"},"1338":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Insert new documents or replace existing ones by `ID`","locale":"en"},"1339":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Update`","locale":"en"},"1340":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Modify specific fields of existing documents by `ID`","locale":"en"},"1341":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Delete`","locale":"en"},"1342":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Delete documents by `ID` or using a scalar filter condition","locale":"en"},"1343":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Query`","locale":"en"},"1344":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Perform vector similarity search or full-text search, optionally combined with scalar filtering and re-ranking","locale":"en"},"1345":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Fetch`","locale":"en"},"1346":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Retrieve full documents directly by `ID`","locale":"en"},"1347":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"`Iterate`","locale":"en"},"1348":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"Stream every document one by one without loading the whole collection into memory","locale":"en"},"1349":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations","content":"All write operations (`insert`, `upsert`, `update`, `delete`) are immediately visible for querying — enabling true real-time, streaming workloads.","locale":"en"},"1350":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"page","content":"Insert","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","locale":"en"},"1351":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Document `Doc`","locale":"en"},"1352":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Insert a Single Document","locale":"en"},"1353":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"Insert a Batch of Documents","locale":"en"},"1354":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Insert Documents with Sparse Vectors","locale":"en"},"1355":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Insert Documents with Multiple Fields and Vectors","locale":"en"},"1356":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","content":"Use the &#x2A;*`insert()`** method to add one or more new documents (`Doc`) to a collection.","locale":"en"},"1357":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","content":"**Performance Tip**:\\\nNew vectors are initially buffered for fast ingestion. For optimal search performance, call `optimize()` after inserting a large batch of documents.","locale":"en"},"1358":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Each `Doc` passed to `insert()` must:","locale":"en"},"1359":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Have a unique `id` (not already present in the collection)","locale":"en"},"1360":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"Provide data that matches the collection's schema:","locale":"en"},"1361":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"**Scalar fields**: provided as key–value pairs under `fields` (scalar field names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1362":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"**Vector embeddings**: provided as key–value pairs under `vectors` (vector names as keys)","locale":"en"},"1363":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"You can omit `nullable` scalar fields if a document doesn't have a value for them","locale":"en"},"1364":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#document-doc","content":"If a document with the same `id` already exists in the collection, the insertion will **fail** for that document.\\\nTo overwrite existing documents or insert without checking, use `upsert()` instead.","locale":"en"},"1365":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"Assume you already have a collection with the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1366":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"A scalar field: `text` (string)","locale":"en"},"1367":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"A dense vector embedding: `text_embedding` (4-dimensional FP32 vector)","locale":"en"},"1368":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"The 4-dimensional vector is for demonstration only — real-world embeddings are usually much larger.","locale":"en"},"1369":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-single-document","content":"You've also opened the collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"1370":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/do