content":"If any document in the batch has incorrect usage (e.g., an unknown field or wrong vector dimension), the method raises an exception and **no documents are inserted**.","locale":"en"},"1377":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"If all documents are valid, the method attempts to insert every one. A failure in one (e.g., duplicate `id`) does **not** stop others from being inserted.","locale":"en"},"1378":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-a-batch-of-documents","content":"🔍 &#x2A;*Always check each `Status` in the result list.**","locale":"en"},"1379":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Assume your collection includes a sparse vector named `sparse_embedding`.","locale":"en"},"1380":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"Insert a document with a sparse vector like this:","locale":"en"},"1381":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-sparse-vectors","content":"A sparse vector is represented as a mapping from `dimension indices` (integers) to `values` (floats).\\\nThere is **no fixed dimension size** — only non-zero dimensions need to be included.","locale":"en"},"1382":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-31","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Real-world applications often require collections with multiple scalar fields and vector embeddings. In this example, assume your collection includes the following schema:","locale":"en"},"1383":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-32","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"**Scalar fields**:","locale":"en"},"1384":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-33","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`book_title` (string)","locale":"en"},"1385":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-34","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`category` (array of strings)","locale":"en"},"1386":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-35","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`publish_year` (32-bit integer)","locale":"en"},"1387":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-36","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"**Vector embeddings**:","locale":"en"},"1388":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-37","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`dense_embedding`: a 768-dimensional dense vector","locale":"en"},"1389":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-38","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"`sparse_embedding`: a sparse vector","locale":"en"},"1390":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/insert#insert-documents-with-multiple-fields-and-vectors","content":"Insert a document with multiple fields and vectors like this:","locale":"en"},"1391":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"page","content":"Iterate","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","locale":"en"},"1392":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"Select Fields and Vectors","locale":"en"},"1393":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Snapshot Semantics","locale":"en"},"1394":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Concurrency","locale":"en"},"1395":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#break-early","content":"Break Early","locale":"en"},"1396":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"Use &#x2A;*`iter_docs()`** to stream **all** documents in a collection one by one.","locale":"en"},"1397":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"Unlike `fetch()` — which retrieves documents by known `id`s — iteration performs a **full scan**. Documents are streamed in bounded windows, so the whole collection is never materialized in memory at once — making it suitable for export, backup, migration, or offline processing.","locale":"en"},"1398":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","content":"The iterator holds a native resource slot on the collection, so let the language close it for you: Python's `with` statement and JavaScript's `for...of` loop both release the iterator when the loop finishes, breaks early, or raises an exception. Iterators also close themselves automatically when fully exhausted.","locale":"en"},"1399":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"By default, every scalar field and every vector is materialized for each document. Use `output_fields` and `include_vector` to reduce the amount of data read:","locale":"en"},"1400":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"**`output_fields`** (`outputFields`): a list of scalar field names to return. If omitted, all scalar fields are returned; an empty list returns no scalar fields. Unknown or duplicate names raise an error.","locale":"en"},"1401":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#select-fields-and-vectors","content":"**`include_vector`** (`includeVector`): whether to materialize vector data. Vectors are included by default; disable it when you only need scalar fields — skipping vectors makes traversal faster.","locale":"en"},"1402":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Both `iter_docs()` and `iterDocsSync()` iterate over an **isolated snapshot taken at call time**:","locale":"en"},"1403":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Data written **after** the iterator is created — inserts, upserts, updates — is **not visible** to this iterator.","locale":"en"},"1404":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Deletes made after creation do not affect the iteration; documents already deleted when the snapshot was taken are filtered out.","locale":"en"},"1405":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"On a writable collection, creating the iterator may seal the current writing segment (each call can produce a new small segment); read-only collections are scanned directly without any write.","locale":"en"},"1406":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#snapshot-semantics","content":"Iteration order is unspecified — it is **not** insertion order, and it can change after `optimize()` reorganizes segments — so never rely on it.","locale":"en"},"1407":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"While any iterator is open on a collection, these operations **raise an error**:","locale":"en"},"1408":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Schema changes — creating or dropping an index, adding, altering or dropping a column","locale":"en"},"1409":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"`optimize()`, which fails at its start","locale":"en"},"1410":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Closing or destroying the collection","locale":"en"},"1411":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Conversely, creating an iterator fails while one of those maintenance operations is already running. Writes, `flush()`, `query()` and `fetch()` remain **unaffected**.","locale":"en"},"1412":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#concurrency","content":"Close every iterator before closing the collection. These restrictions are lifted as soon as all open iterators are closed.","locale":"en"},"1413":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/iterate#break-early","content":"Stopping before the end is safe — exiting the `with` block or the `for...of` loop releases the iterator's slot. When you drive the iterator manually instead, close it yourself:","locale":"en"},"1414":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"page","content":"Update","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","locale":"en"},"1415":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#document-doc","content":"Document `Doc`","locale":"en"},"1416":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-single-document","content":"Update a Single Document","locale":"en"},"1417":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update#update-a-batch-of-documents","content":"Update a Batch of Documents","locale":"en"},"1418":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"Use `update()` to modify **existing** documents (`Doc`).","locale":"en"},"1419":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"Only the scalar fields and vector embeddings you **include will be updated**; all other content remains unchanged.","locale":"en"},"1420":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update","content":"The method accepts either a single `Doc` object or a list of `Doc` objects.","locale":"en"},"1421":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/update-6","page_i