ecific configuration. See the configuration sections for each tokenizer and token filter.","locale":"en"},"2109":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-39","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#ftsindexparam-parameters","content":"Zvec supports **FTS-only collections** — you can create a collection with text fields and no vector fields at all.","locale":"en"},"2110":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-40","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#performing-full-text-search","content":"Zvec provides two query modes for full-text search, both using the `Fts` object within a `Query`:","locale":"en"},"2111":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-41","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#performing-full-text-search","content":"**Match String** — natural language input, automatically tokenized","locale":"en"},"2112":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-42","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#performing-full-text-search","content":"**Query String** — advanced expression syntax with boolean operators","locale":"en"},"2113":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-43","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#match-string","content":"Use `match_string` for natural language queries. The input is plain text — no special syntax or escaping is needed. It is tokenized using the same tokenizer configured on the field, and tokens are combined using the default operator (`OR` by default).","locale":"en"},"2114":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-44","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#match-string","content":"With the default `OR` operator, this returns documents containing **either** \"machine\" **or** \"learning\" (or both), ranked by BM25 relevance.","locale":"en"},"2115":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-45","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#query-string","content":"Use `query_string` for advanced queries with explicit boolean operators, required/excluded terms, and exact phrase matching.","locale":"en"},"2116":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-46","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#query-string","content":"This query requires \"learning\", excludes \"neural\", and matches the exact phrase \"vector search\".","locale":"en"},"2117":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-47","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#query-string","content":"`query_string` and `match_string` are **mutually exclusive** — you must provide exactly one of them in each `Fts` object.","locale":"en"},"2118":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-48","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#query-syntax-reference","content":"The following operators are supported in `query_string` expressions:","locale":"en"},"2119":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-49","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#query-syntax-reference","content":"Syntax","locale":"en"},"2120":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts-50","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/fts#query-syntax-reference","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"2121":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-ope