,"locale":"en"},"2409":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"2410":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Performing Multi-Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2411":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Re-ranking Strategies","locale":"en"},"2412":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","content":"Zvec supports **multi-vector queries**, allowing you to combine different embeddings in a single search.","locale":"en"},"2413":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","content":"When querying multiple vector embeddings, Zvec retrieves candidates from each vector space independently and then fuses them into one relevance-ordered list. Because scores from different vector spaces might not be directly comparable, you must choose a suitable **re-ranking strategy**.","locale":"en"},"2414":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes:","locale":"en"},"2415":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"You have opened a `collection` with multiple vector fields","locale":"en"},"2416":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"You're familiar with the basic vector querying concepts. If not, please review the single-vector search guide","locale":"en"},"2417":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"This example collection contains two vector fields:","locale":"en"},"2418":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`dense_embedding`** — A 768-dimensional dense vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2419":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`sparse_embedding`** — A sparse vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2420":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#prerequisites","content":"It also includes two scalar fields (`publish_year` and `category`).","locale":"en"},"2421":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"In Python, pass a list of query specifications to `query()` and provide a fusion strategy through `reranker`. In Node.js, pass the sub-queries to `multiQuerySync()` or `multiQuery()` and configure `rerank`.","locale":"en"},"2422":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"This example queries both `dense_embedding` and `sparse_embedding` and uses `WeightedReRanker` to combine their results. Weights are positional and must follow the same order as `queries`.","locale":"en"},"2423":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"`topk` always controls the number of **final documents** returned after fusion.","locale":"en"},"2424":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Python does not currently expose a separate candidate-count option for each sub-query in `Collection.query()`.","locale":"en"},"2425":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"Node.js supports `numCandidates` on each sub-query. If omitted, its default is `max(topk, 10)`.","locale":"en"},"2426":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-17","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#performing-multi-vector-search","content":"`topn` is used only when calling a re-ranker's standalone `rerank()` method; it is not a constructor argument.","locale":"en"},"2427":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-18","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Zvec provides different re-ranking strategies to combine scores from multiple vector fields.","locale":"en"},"2428":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-19","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Re-ranker","locale":"en"},"2429":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-20","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`WeightedReRanker`","locale":"en"},"2430":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-21","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`RrfReRanker` (Reciprocal Rank Fusion)","locale":"en"},"2431":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-22","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Approach","locale":"en"},"2432":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-23","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Combines normalized similarity scores using **custom weights**","locale":"en"},"2433":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-24","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Fuses results based only on **ranking positions** — no scores needed  With a zero-based rank *r* (the first result is 0), the RRF score is: $\\text{RRF}(r) = \\frac{1}{k + r + 1}$","locale":"en"},"2434":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-25","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Best for","locale":"en"},"2435":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-26","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"• Scores are reasonably comparable across vector fields  • You know the relative importance of each embedding type","locale":"en"},"2436":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-27","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"• Scores come from different metrics or scales  • You prefer a simple, robust, tuning-free method","locale":"en"},"2437":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-28","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"2438":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-29","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`weights`: An ordered list aligned with `queries`. Score normalization uses each queried field's schema.","locale":"en"},"2439":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector-30","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/multi-vector#re-ranking-strategies","content":"`rank_constant` (*k*): Controls how quickly rank influence decreases. Higher values reduce the dominance of top-ranked results.","locale":"en"},"2440":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"page","content":"Single Vector","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Products","Zvec","Guides","Data Operations","Query"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","locale":"en"},"2441":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-0","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites","locale":"en"},"2442":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-1","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"Performing Single-Vector Search","locale":"en"},"2443":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-2","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#parameters","content":"Parameters","locale":"en"},"2444":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-3","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#common-parameters","content":"Common Parameters","locale":"en"},"2445":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-4","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#index-specific-parameters","content":"Index-Specific Parameters","locale":"en"},"2446":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-5","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","content":"Single-vector search finds documents most similar to a single query embedding. This is the most common search pattern in vector databases.","locale":"en"},"2447":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-6","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"This guide assumes you have opened a collection and have a `collection` object ready.","locale":"en"},"2448":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-7","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"This example collection contains two vector fields:","locale":"en"},"2449":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-8","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`dense_embedding`** — A 768-dimensional dense vector using cosine metric","locale":"en"},"2450":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-9","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"**`sparse_embedding`** — A sparse vector using inner product metric","locale":"en"},"2451":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-10","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#prerequisites","content":"It also includes two scalar fields (`publish_year` and `category`).","locale":"en"},"2452":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-11","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"To perform a single-vector similarity search, use the `query()` method and provide a single query specification.","locale":"en"},"2453":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-12","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"All queries return a `list[Doc]` containing the **top-k** most similar documents, sorted by relevance score.","locale":"en"},"2454":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-13","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"Each `Doc` object includes:","locale":"en"},"2455":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-14","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"`id`: The document identifier.","locale":"en"},"2456":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-15","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"`score`: The similarity score.","locale":"en"},"2457":{"id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector-16","page_id":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/db/data-operations/query/single-vector#performing-single-vector-search","content":"`vectors`: A map from vector field names to their corresponding embedding values.\\\nThis is